<article class="env-lemma" id="0AJT">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AJT">Lemma <span data-tag="0AJT">15.86.11</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a ring. Let $K_ j \in D(R)$, $j = 1, 2, 3$ with $H^ i(K_ j) = 0$ for $i \not\in \{ -1, 0\} $. Let $\varphi : K_1 \to K_2$ and $\psi : K_2 \to K_3$ be maps in $D(R)$. If $H^0(\varphi ) = 0$ and $H^{-1}(\psi ) = 0$, then $\varphi \circ \psi = 0$. </p>
</article> 
</p>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Apply Derived Categories, Lemma <a href="/tag/08Q2" data-tag="08Q2">13.12.5</a> to see that $\varphi \circ \psi $ factors through $\tau _{\leq -2}K_2 = 0$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>
